            <ArticleTitle>Transcatheter closure of left coronary cameral fistula with Amplatzer duct occluder II.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>265-7</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>The surgical and transcatheter coil closure of coronary arterial fistulas are described in the literature. We report our experience with the successful transcatheter closure of a coronary arterial fistula, arising from the left coronary artery and draining into the right ventricle, with the new Amplatzer duct occluder II device.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
